Subject: [PATCH] EM app: the HAL's transmit power reading no longer overwrites the radio's percentage

When the monitor was ready the EM app read each radio's transmit power from the
HAL (wifi_hal_getRadioTransmitPower, in dBm) and stored it in the radio's
TransmitPower, TR-181's percentage of the maximum: Device.WiFi.Radio.{i}.
TransmitPower then read 20, 30 or 33 on radios configured at 100, and the next
radio configuration applied set that as a percentage. A reading of 0 was stored
as 100.

The reading is now recorded as the radio's measured transmit power in dBm
(0043), which the radio subdoc carries to the co-located EasyMesh agent;
TransmitPower keeps its configured percentage. A reading of 0 is no reading.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/source/apps/em/wifi_em.c
+++ b/source/apps/em/wifi_em.c
@@ -3180,7 +3180,6 @@ void handle_em_command_event(wifi_app_t *app, wifi_event_t *event)
     case wifi_event_type_notify_monitor_done:
         is_monitor_done = TRUE;
         {
-            wifi_mgr_t *wifi_mgr = get_wifimgr_obj();
             unsigned int num_radios = getNumberRadios();
             for (unsigned int i = 0; i < num_radios; i++) {
                 ULONG curr_txpower = 0;
@@ -3191,15 +3190,16 @@ void handle_em_command_event(wifi_app_t *app, wifi_event_t *event)
                     continue;
                 }
                 if (curr_txpower == 0) {
-                    wifi_util_error_print(WIFI_EM, "%s:%d: tx power reported as 0 for radio_index=%u; defaulting to 100\n",
+                    wifi_util_error_print(WIFI_EM, "%s:%d: tx power reported as 0 for radio_index=%u; no reading\n",
                         __func__, __LINE__, i);
-                    curr_txpower = 100;
+                    continue;
                 }
 
-                pthread_mutex_lock(&wifi_mgr->data_cache_lock);
-                wifi_mgr->radio_config[i].oper.transmitPower = (UINT)curr_txpower;
-                pthread_mutex_unlock(&wifi_mgr->data_cache_lock);
-                wifi_util_info_print(WIFI_EM, "%s:%d: radio_index=%u curr_txpower=%lu\n",
+                // The HAL's reading is in dBm. The radio's TransmitPower is TR-181's
+                // percentage, its configured value, and stays as it is: the reading
+                // travels beside it (TransmitPowerdBm in the radio subdoc).
+                webconfig_set_radio_tx_power_dbm(i, (int)curr_txpower, true);
+                wifi_util_info_print(WIFI_EM, "%s:%d: radio_index=%u curr_txpower=%lu dBm\n",
                     __func__, __LINE__, i, curr_txpower);
             }
         }
